I am experiencing some issues with a RocketRAID 2760A card using the
mvsas driver.  The RocketRAID2760A has 3 Marvell 88SE9485 controllers
and an integral PCIe switch, yielding a total of 24 SAS ports without
the use of SAS expanders.

At boot time I've been having some problems with drives not being
available when mounts happen.  The first thing we tried was forcing
mvsas in to the initramfs to get it to load earlier - that helped a
great deal but the root cause of the issues seems to be that the first
series of commands sent to the controller are timing out.  Subsequent
commands work fine, and the controller behaves properly after that. 
I've done around 100TB of I/O after boot without any issue whatsoever so
I kind of suspect the issues are caused by the card not being properly
initialized somehow.  All 18 of the drives I have connected currently
get from 1-4 command timeouts on the first bit of I/O.  The drives are
all SATA.

I have tested this behavior and it occurs on the Ubuntu-supplied 3.2 and
3.5 kernels as well as the Ubuntu mainline 3.6.11 kernel.  Currently I
am running on 3.5.0-21-generic #32.

As soon as the first I/O happens (after device discovery - that part at
least is successful), I get errors like this (full dmesg attached):

